(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Writing Mathematics in Notebooks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"36e881d8-3949-44a8-8925-2be5927017a4"],

Cell["MathNotebook Tutorial", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"9813f150-4a9e-4c86-84dc-cff152d574dc"],

Cell["\<\
How to write a mathematics paper in a Wolfram notebook: journal stylesheets, \
live referencing, and conversion between LaTeX source and native typeset \
math. Whether the mathematics is written as LaTeX or as built-in typeset math \
is your choice throughout \[LongDash] the palette only moves a selection from \
one to the other.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"5bb00ad4-48ad-44d2-a69b-7f9934bc39ea"],

Cell["Getting Started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"93c3ce4a-96f0-48ee-b609-d6364c97501e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After installing the paclet, restart the front end so that ",
 StyleBox["Palettes \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the stylesheet menu appear."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"dcb55a7a-442f-459b-8a71-5889bd03a951"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Give a notebook a journal style with ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Stylesheet \[RightArrow] MathNotebook",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", or the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Apply stylesheet",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu; ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in that menu takes it back."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b22cc6c5-4983-4b8c-afad-3e4ac8ec4f46"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Style the opening cells ",
 StyleBox["Title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then write in ",
 StyleBox["Section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0216bc86-3cf3-4301-b2b3-271bb5db0446"],

Cell["\<\
Every palette button acts on the notebook you were last editing, and on its \
current selection.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9844922e-77af-456c-911a-910ff2342313"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The journal stylesheets are light-only; applying one from the palette\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group also sets the notebook to light mode, so printed and exported output \
matches the screen. Applying a sheet clears the two size overrides below it, \
the new sheet replacing them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6b64e0ce-cea7-4672-a92a-e9b6867274db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Update from cloud",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Setup",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, asks the Wolfram Cloud which version is published and installs it \
only when it is newer than the one you have \[LongDash] so checking costs a \
line of text, not a download. It then rebuilds the front end menus and \
reopens the palette, which makes the new palette, stylesheets and tutorial \
live immediately."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d611a5f5-d042-4058-8a97-bab3526d3cfd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It always says which of three things happened: updated, with the old and \
new version numbers; already current; or the cloud could not be reached. \
Kernel code from the new version loads after ",
 StyleBox["Evaluation \[RightArrow] Quit Kernel",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] the button will not quit the kernel out from under your \
session."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b239f865-5344-45f1-b552-d876544e5385"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A copy loaded from a development directory shadows anything installed from \
the cloud, so the button reports that and downloads nothing. The same check \
from code: ",
 StyleBox["UpdateMathNotebook[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"686e1bbf-d6f8-46d2-8c4b-a0daa0fef554"],

Cell["Referencing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"16dfa148-e4d6-4af3-9b14-fa3ec385cc95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Select a numbered cell \[LongDash] an equation, a theorem, a section, a \
numbered item \[LongDash] and press ",
 StyleBox["Copy reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", then paste into your text."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8effc931-0190-4f64-a73d-cbcf8c4cb69c"],

Cell["\<\
The pasted reference is a live button showing the current number, so \
reordering cells renumbers every reference to them.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"895e400c-4371-4a89-bf3b-8db6b29f88e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Clicking a reference jumps to its target; ",
 StyleBox["\[UpArrow] Go back",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns to where you clicked from."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a60e7ffc-b4da-49ec-8534-aa8ea26ddf0c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", in the ",
 StyleBox["Blocks",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group, adds a bibliography entry: it asks for a citation key and puts a \
tagged, labelled entry at the end of the bibliography \[LongDash] starting \
one, under a ",
 StyleBox["References",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " heading, if the notebook has none yet. It goes there rather than at the \
cursor, unlike every other button in that group."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0ccc05a4-ec37-45a9-943b-3a5d6615e596"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Insert citation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " then offers everything the notebook has tagged, literature entries and \
numbered blocks in two lists, with a filter field; picking one inserts a red \
bracketed link to it. Type a key the notebook does not have and it cites that \
instead, so a citation can be written before its target exists. To name a \
cell yourself, use ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Cell Tags",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"eeb3e950-5cc5-4752-8ea8-628cdfec8337"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A citation to a numbered environment shows its number instead of its tag: \
tag a theorem, cite it, and the citation reads ",
 StyleBox["Theorem 1.1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] renumbering itself when cells move, in the exported PDF as on \
screen. A tag no cell carries yet keeps its brackets, so a citation written \
before its target is still readable."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d5930f2a-db45-4cd3-bb43-5c06504b1933"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tagging a ",
 StyleBox["Reference",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell also labels it: the entry shows its tag in brackets in the margin, \
which is exactly what a citation to it reads, so the bibliography and the \
body agree without your typing either."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"519af52e-5f47-4b71-b2b4-7bf1c85dad45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Cell Tags dialog sets the tag and not the label, so after tagging an \
entry that way press ",
 StyleBox["Refresh labels",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] it labels every entry of the notebook at once, and clears the \
label of an entry whose tag you removed. From code, ",
 StyleBox["LabelReferences[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0897e51d-c8c0-429d-8d9b-e01a2d2c2b29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Sort bibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reorders the entries: by first citation, which is what BibTeX\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s unsrt prints, by key, or by the entry text. ",
 StyleBox["Report uncited",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sorts nothing and answers the question a sort cannot \[LongDash] which \
entries nothing cites, and which citations point at no cell. Where the \
entries came from a ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", the order shown is the notebook\[CloseCurlyQuote]s alone: that file and \
its style decide what the compiled paper prints."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7b422871-39a1-44d4-a301-eb81ca8885db"],

Cell["\<\
The theorem below and the equation after it are practice targets: select \
either one and copy a reference to it.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"218f1fbc-cdf1-4dea-b8c1-830059a4bc31"],

Cell["The exponential map is surjective onto the unit circle.", "Theorem",ExpressionUUID->"86df50d9-effe-4f84-acbb-b3d5bbbe428e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", "\[Pi]"}]], "+", "1", "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"083a2f64-ce5d-\
4a0a-b63d-103dbc80524e"],

Cell["Stylesheets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"98afea76-3f8b-4cbf-8d7c-4f0be598f40e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four templates: ",
 StyleBox["AMSArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (amsart, Palatino), ",
 StyleBox["ArXivArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (article, Latin Modern), ",
 StyleBox["SpringerJournal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["RevTeXAPS",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " (Times)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"957a62e8-6e44-44fa-9aaa-58ead2936126"],

Cell["\<\
All four define the same style names, so switching between them is instant \
and changes nothing but the typography.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2d13d23e-e8aa-44e4-be8e-2ba129bb9871"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PlainArticle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a fifth sheet and not a template: it is the notebook's own typography \
with the paper structure added, and it is what an imported paper opens on \
when its \\documentclass names no journal above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"df4d7345-f20d-41fc-9f60-bd55781f47db"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem, Lemma, Proposition, Corollary, Conjecture, Claim, Definition, \
Example, Construction, Remark, Question, and Observation share a single \
counter that resets at each section, exactly as in LaTeX; numbered equations \
count continuously through the document.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"811e32fd-8be3-46e0-9432-acbd546deeb4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Insert environments from the palette's ",
 StyleBox["Insert environment",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " menu, or with the ",
 StyleBox["Proof",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["Equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["Equation (n)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c568d23d-92f6-48b8-8fc9-633a5579c774"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern and TeX Gyre are LaTeX fonts, not system fonts: press ",
 StyleBox["Install LaTeX fonts",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " once to copy them out of a local TeX distribution (",
 ButtonBox["tug.org/texlive",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 ") into your user font directory, then restart the front end. They are \
installed for the whole machine, not inside Mathematica, so any application \
can use them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b9f9219e-d83c-40e6-910d-69a3f35d87fd"],

Cell["Reading and Writing Comfortably", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"20668270-bc8d-4012-b2b9-0ff24ba63f78"],

Cell["\<\
Each palette group folds: click its opener or its name to collapse it, so \
only the buttons you are using take up room. The palette remembers which \
groups are open across front end restarts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a6deed77-ecfb-4fdb-b751-4d000dc63651"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Document view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group holds two sliders and a reset. Like every other palette control they \
act on the notebook you were last editing, so leave the palette open beside \
your paper and drag while you read it."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b9c3f864-907c-4d2d-b3ab-e04346bba3b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Text size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sets the size of ",
 StyleBox["Text",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and scales the rest of the prose with it \[LongDash] the title, the \
headings, the abstract, the theorem environments, proofs, bibliography \
entries, and both kinds of list \[LongDash] so the document keeps its \
proportions instead of one style growing alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"12ba7fc1-6d58-4d2d-9b26-323fba120c7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " does the same for displayed equations and their numbers, independently of \
the prose \[LongDash] the usual reason to reach for it is an equation left \
too small to read beside text you have just enlarged."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4ecaad7c-055f-462d-ab24-38b7633042c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both set real font sizes, so they reach the exported PDF. ",
 StyleBox["Format \[RightArrow] Magnification",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is a different thing entirely \[LongDash] it zooms the screen and never \
changes print."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"101508b0-7c9c-4a88-9150-89e2ce34d9a9"],

Cell["\<\
The settings are stored in the notebook itself, so they survive saving and \
reopening and travel with the file to a coauthor.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"aa96c262-206c-4a1e-9162-8fd5035824d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reset view",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " returns the notebook to its stylesheet defaults and leaves no trace of the \
overrides; applying a stylesheet clears them too, since the new sheet \
replaces them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6cd92070-45c9-4b29-babc-fbaeb740c453"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX cells are images and cannot inherit a style, so ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " re-renders each of them through LaTeX at the new size, from the TeX the \
cell stores."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6229ccce-a291-4dd9-9551-bf9163f432d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["SetDocumentFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["SetMathFontSize[nb, 16]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] each takes ",
 StyleBox["Automatic",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop its own override \[LongDash] and ",
 StyleBox["ResetDocumentView[nb]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to drop all of them. They work on a notebook still using ",
 StyleBox["Default",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " too."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"03a3f2b6-0fa6-4e4a-acd4-c926bab50dca"],

Cell["Math Input Shortcuts", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bcafab02-88e9-49b3-86a6-9ee26a1f6f6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " inline math in text, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+0",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exits."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c768788d-3bb6-4552-88e9-5edf25d62377"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+/",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fraction, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " square root."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f9d9042a-9293-4792-b9c7-3ae201d37767"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+^",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " superscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+_",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " subscript, ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+%",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " switches between them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6b5e1417-63d3-493f-89e5-4aa3e0d0305c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["name",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["esc",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " enters symbols: ",
 StyleBox["a",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Alpha], ",
 StyleBox["el",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Element], ",
 StyleBox["->",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[RightArrow] \[Rule]."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4346044f-38b9-4e56-b872-880cd3c8399e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " shows the cell expression (",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+E",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " on Windows)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4c4ad4bd-d397-4b67-802d-c48062af5bb4"],

Cell["Working with Cells", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f5a16ed8-5d89-41b1-810c-cac1321a8296"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Click a cell bracket to select the cell; drag across brackets to select \
several; ",
 StyleBox["Delete",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " removes them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"382154f2-5e3c-41af-867e-4f894d9464d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " extends the selection outward; repeat to reach the whole cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e20ac1cf-8f12-474d-9e14-fd9f80320722"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["9",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " restyle a cell: Title, Section, Subsection, Text, Input."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"faf5cc9d-35f2-4b71-ac11-25a278886441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+D",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " divides a cell at the cursor; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+M",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " merges selected cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9b7420a7-4a1d-4bdc-b400-512c05e93eea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Ctrl+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " groups selected cells; ",
 StyleBox["Ctrl+Shift+G",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ungroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0c552d6c-f318-4caa-a760-0aa0c6faa69e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Double-click a group bracket to close or open the group; ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+{",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["Cmd+Shift+}",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " open and close all subgroups."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fc628aab-97ca-41a6-83f5-21d8238596f0"],

Cell["\<\
Double-click a closed group's remaining bracket to reopen it; use Cell \
\[RightArrow] Delete All Output before sharing a notebook.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6c91f5a0-2bf7-4cb7-a69b-4220c409e6f1"],

Cell["LaTeX Conversion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a569ff89-9f82-4a46-9d9b-7d340710cb41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["Import & Export",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group is the route for a paper; the ",
 StyleBox["Selection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group acts on the cells you have selected. Hover any button for a sentence \
on what it does."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ba0fdc73-a5c0-4686-9256-9425076772c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Import .tex file\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads a whole paper into a new notebook: ",
 StyleBox["\\section",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and the theorem-like environments the preamble declares become cells of \
the matching style, mathematics is typeset, ",
 StyleBox["\\label",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes a cell tag, and ",
 StyleBox["\\ref",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\cite",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become live links. Anything it does not convert is carried verbatim, so \
what it cannot read it also does not damage."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a5600a47-bc7e-4b9e-85d8-6be6e21c0303"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The front matter comes with it: ",
 StyleBox["\\title",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\author",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\date",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Title, Author and Date cells you can edit \[LongDash] the edit \
reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[LongDash] and an ",
 StyleBox["abstract",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes Abstract cells, headed once however many paragraphs it runs to. ",
 StyleBox["\\maketitle",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " has no content of its own, so it stays as text beside ",
 StyleBox["\\sloppy",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\tableofcontents",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1c24aebb-bb6f-4015-9244-54a3153136f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["itemize",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["enumerate",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["description",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become Item and ItemNumbered cells, one per ",
 StyleBox["\\item",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", nesting into Subitem and Subsubitem. Each list restarts its numbering as \
LaTeX does, an ",
 StyleBox["\\item[label]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " prints the label instead of the number, and a second paragraph of one item \
becomes an ItemParagraph cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"364f892c-bcdc-4566-980d-88a0af30c73b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["figure",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes its caption plus an ",
 StyleBox["Input",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " cell holding the code that draws the picture \[LongDash] an ",
 StyleBox["Import",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the file the paper shipped, which you replace with the Wolfram code \
that generates it. Evaluate the cell and the figure is live; the picture's \
own markup, TikZ included, still goes back into the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " untouched, so the generating code stays the notebook's alone."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"31f88c65-e344-4c46-8ca0-25d84eb7c7f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bibliography comes in whichever way the paper writes it. A ",
 StyleBox["thebibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " becomes one Reference cell per ",
 StyleBox["\\bibitem",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", each showing its key in brackets exactly as the citations to it read, and \
each is yours to edit \[LongDash] the edit reaches the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Entries pulled from a ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " become the same cells, but there the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " stays the source of truth: only the ",
 StyleBox["\\bibliography",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands go back out, so edit the ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and re-import. A declared ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that is not beside the ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is reported rather than passed over in silence."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"222128b8-91d1-4d77-8b2b-31225ab01658"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export to .tex\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes the whole notebook back out as a paper. An imported one comes back \
as the source it was read from, edits and all; a notebook you wrote here \
comes out as LaTeX built from its styles. This is the export route \
\[LongDash] the two buttons below are for a handful of cells, not for a \
submission."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b0f31430-90d9-4425-a0bd-32bcc2c17040"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export submission\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " writes the paper into a directory instead of into a file, and puts \
everything it needs to compile beside it: each figure file the ",
 StyleBox["\\includegraphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands name, each ",
 StyleBox[".bib",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " the preamble declares, and \[LongDash] where a local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is found \[LongDash] the ",
 StyleBox[".bbl",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", which arXiv needs because it runs LaTeX but does not run BibTeX. That \
directory is the upload. A ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " on its own names files that stayed behind and compiles nowhere but the \
paper's original directory, which is the whole reason this button exists \
beside the one above."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"25ce5848-5794-46ae-bdfc-ff6ac5328f49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nothing arXiv rejects goes into it: no ",
 StyleBox[".aux",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox[".log",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and no compiled PDF \[LongDash] the LaTeX run happens in a scratch copy \
and only the ",
 StyleBox[".bbl",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " comes back. A file the paper names that is not on disk is reported by \
name, never quietly left out and never re-rendered from the notebook: the \
format and size the ",
 StyleBox["\\includegraphics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " assumes are not recoverable, and guessing them would be guessing at how \
you compile."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"41197259-f853-4558-aaa5-cd8be8a704ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Per-cell conversion has no button of its own \[LongDash] the whole-paper \
route above is the way out to LaTeX \[LongDash] but the two functions remain: \
",
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " reads the selected cells as LaTeX and replaces the mathematics in them \
with editable typeset math, and ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " turns it back into LaTeX you can read or paste elsewhere. With nothing \
selected, the whole notebook."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"03cc02e0-4c20-466a-b15c-c7e4a51d4947"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " parses inline ",
 StyleBox["$\[Ellipsis]$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\\(\[Ellipsis]\\)",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and displayed ",
 StyleBox["$$\[Ellipsis]$$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\\[\[Ellipsis]\\]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["equation",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "; the starred forms stay unnumbered, the unstarred ones become numbered \
equations."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1add3f7e-9cea-4fd8-a1fe-7fa791cd40c2"],

Cell["\<\
A display environment written inside a paragraph, with prose on the lines \
around it, is lifted out into its own equation cell and the prose stays in \
Text cells on either side.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f25d69b2-7d0f-40d6-a92e-b33e49a1188d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 StyleBox["align",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " environment becomes a grid aligned on its ",
 StyleBox["&",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", so it stays editable as one equation cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"337d9fd7-9fde-4a94-95fd-cc2063e1374a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each converted cell keeps its original TeX, so ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back what you typed rather than a re-serialization of the boxes. \
Anything the parser cannot read is left untouched."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"40701f9c-b8c7-4e31-bf42-977a8d820ec9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Input, Code, and Output cells are skipped, so ",
 StyleBox["$",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in code is safe."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d0e03769-84ee-4834-b13e-c46115ff8352"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same from code, on any notebook: ",
 StyleBox["ImportLaTeXDocument[\"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXDocument[nb, \"paper.tex\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["ExportLaTeXBundle[nb, \"directory\"]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for the whole paper, ",
 StyleBox["ConvertLaTeXCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["ConvertMathCells[]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for a selection."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5d08161f-7639-4124-85ca-ca0d1e1c0ae5"],

Cell["MaTeX", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e29ffd2e-d8bd-4a95-a61d-d8614c3c6d05"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "MaTeX (",
 ButtonBox["github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"],
 ") is optional, and needs a TeX distribution and Ghostscript. It is used \
only by the two ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " buttons in the ",
 StyleBox["Selection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " group; referencing, stylesheets, and LaTeX conversion do not."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e3acdf7c-3ad2-44e0-ad5c-83a0d10d7a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use it when an equation has to come out of real LaTeX \[LongDash] macros, \
",
 StyleBox["tikz-cd",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " diagrams, exact journal metrics."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ec358155-3628-4a35-a309-fb555471075a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Install MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " installs the paclet and points it at the local ",
 StyleBox["pdflatex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gs",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f649f100-1149-4bc5-a27f-ea6b78329e2f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["math \[Rule] MaTeX",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " sends the selected display equations through LaTeX, at whatever size ",
 StyleBox["Math size",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " is showing mathematics at; ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gives back editable typeset math from the TeX stored in each cell."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1044fb7d-5b29-4aff-a758-bbd81ea991da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MaTeX preferences",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " opens your ",
 StyleBox["init.m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " in the front end \[LongDash] deliberately not through the system handler \
for ",
 StyleBox[".m",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " files. Set the preamble, the magnification, and ",
 StyleBox["$useMaTeXQ = True",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to route TeX typed into a notebook through LaTeX instead of the built-in \
parser."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ef2df277-203c-414b-9cf6-4d8700483b3b"],

Cell["\<\
MaTeX cells are images: convert them back before editing, and keep rendering \
for last.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8e10e0fd-537a-4c99-a21a-02b0f39673a8"],

Cell["Best Practices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c3dd4451-261c-46d0-8c36-88326b914200"],

Cell["\<\
One environment per cell, inserted from the palette, keeps the styles and \
counters consistent.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"24bbe3d7-1ee7-40f0-9bb0-c70700c9fdea"],

Cell["\<\
Tag cells as you write them; tagging a theorem after fifty pages means \
finding it again.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"29603fef-bbb9-4628-9b37-171b1ea1a78d"],

Cell["\<\
Do not strip cell tagging rules: they hold the TeX source that makes the \
round trip lossless.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2996d750-f3aa-4046-9ebe-5aa5bb763159"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Export to .tex\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " at submission time, not continuously \[LongDash] the notebook is the \
source. Use ",
 StyleBox["Export submission\[Ellipsis]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " when the destination is arXiv: a ",
 StyleBox[".tex",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " alone is not a submission."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4592199c-799b-4290-9c11-0487c0b4e2d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before sharing: ",
 StyleBox["Cell \[RightArrow] Delete All Output",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["MaTeX \[Rule] math",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " the MaTeX cells so a coauthor can edit them."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1d713636-b81d-4eff-aa34-a3ac60340fe4"],

Cell["Credits", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d67c6c18-e948-4417-8980-0d253806aa65"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The referencing scheme and the MaTeX integration are originally due to Nik \
Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"],
 "; this paclet packages and extends that work."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e501ed1-b1d0-4d09-9fdb-2d6c53187ab0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nik Murzin, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/sw1sh",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/sw1sh"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/sw1sh"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[murzin]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"murzin",ExpressionUUID->"71d9dbde-f6f3-4091-91a2-da7940f38552"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Szabolcs Horvat, MaTeX: LaTeX labels in Mathematica, ",
 ButtonBox["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://github.com/szhorvat/MaTeX"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[matex]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"matex",ExpressionUUID->"a23a7f37-529b-45c0-9ce3-f2158e51df4a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "TeX Live, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/texlive/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/texlive/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/texlive/"],
 " \[LongDash] on macOS, MacTeX, ",
 ButtonBox["https://tug.org/mactex/",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://tug.org/mactex/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://tug.org/mactex/"]
}], "Reference",
 CellDingbat->Cell[
   TextData["[texlive]"]],
 ParagraphIndent->0,
 CellTags->"texlive",ExpressionUUID->"9b22a58a-ebbc-40ba-98bc-e29242910aa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Latin Modern, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://ctan.org/pkg/lm"],
 " and TeX Gyre, ",
 ButtonBox["https://ctan.org/pkg/tex-gyre",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
